<title>NEW ZEALAND: RBNZ rejects bids on 42-day T-Bills.</title>
<headline>RBNZ rejects bids on 42-day T-Bills.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1996-09-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Reserve Bank of New Zealand said on Tuesday it rejected bids for $100 million of 42-day seasonal Treasury bills.</p>
<p>Asked to comment, a spokesman said it was a &quot;commercial decision&quot;.  </p>
<p>The weighted average yield on $100 million of 104-day bills was 9.675 percent, with bids totalling $530 million.</p>
<p>The weighted average yield on $100 million of 126-day bills was 9.639 percent, with bids totalling $405 million.</p>
<p>-- Wellington newsroom 64 4 473-4746</p>
